  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, concat) is the best result so far at 0.688 acc / 0.659 F1, showing that multimodal fusion adds ~3.5 points over the best RNA-only config (0.653). The only untested design dimension in this top-performing setup is the fusion strategy (concat vs. weighted). Question: Does weighted fusion outperform simple concatenation when combining the (relatively weak) image signal with the strong RNA signal? Rationale: This is a clean one-variable A/B test against the current best, making the result fully interpretable. If weighted fusion helps, it gives an immediate performance gain and suggests the model benefits from learned modality balancing; if not, we confirm concat is sufficient and can redirect budget toward the image-encoder question (ViT-L vs. ResNet50). Under a limited budget, resolving this binary design choice in the context of the strongest configuration is the highest-information-per-experiment next step."
}

